- Final combined lifecycle group including actual native text + voice, runtime,
  simulation selection, and assistant settings: 89 passed, 61 SDK deprecation
  warnings, `APPLICATION_GUARD_BLOCKED_ATTEMPTS=0`.

Recovery and parity continuation:
- Added optimistic compare-and-swap snapshots in the existing FlowSession store.
  Recovery pins root and active flow-version identity plus exact source digests,
  tenant/property/call scope, current node, explicit caller provenance and safe
  projections. Scope drift, version replacement, stale writes and a snapshot
  pending an uncommitted effect fail closed. A committed action result resumes
  from its recorded branch without replaying the external effect; terminal
  effects are persisted pending and are never replayed after an ambiguous exit.
- Call admission loads recovery before current-version selection, reconstructs
  the pinned historical version, and refuses changed source digests. Recovery
  uses the existing FlowSession JSONB field (SQLite JSON variant only for the
  in-memory ORM fixture); no new persistence service or provider was introduced.
- Form collection now exposes later fields as optional model arguments while
  requiring the configured current field. Each optional value must be present
  in the current caller transcript and pass its own native validator before any
  facts mutate. It preserves ordered prompts for missing fields and accepts
  valid same-turn answers instead of forcing redundant caller turns.
- Actual Pipecat STT-to-FlowManager-to-model-tool-to-TTS test now canonicalizes
  caller "tomorrow" to the injected next-day date before an action sees facts.
  The same real worker test supplies name and email in one caller utterance;
  both explicit values are accepted, and an invented optional email is rejected.
- Recovery ORM coverage exercises round-trip identity, stale CAS and scope
  mismatch. Runtime coverage proves pending action is not replayed and a
  committed action's branch resumes without calling it again.

